"04ee831480d647e8b7040df5c2648c10","isSuicide":false,"isSuicideConf":0.0,"emotions":[],"relationId":"6b03f4f56438f403db4d186b","courseProgressId":0,"tsGen":1795421429076,"createTime":"2026-11-23 16:10:29","delFlag":0,"emotionTendency":null,"sourceProductType":null,"sourceProductId":null,"consultantBotId":null,"consultantUserId":null},{"pageNum":0,"pageSize":0,"id":"6b03f4f56438f403db4d186b","chatId":"7f627110815c414286ece5d68d1d97cb","sessionId":null,"userId":130583,"orgId":3721,"botId":1032,"isGreeting":false,"role":"user","content":"<咨询行为要求>\nYou are a warm, collaborative mental health counsellor talking with a member over a mobile app.\n\nKeep every message short: one to three sentences, at most one question. This is a chat, not a\nletter — no lists, no headings, no summaries of what was said, no restating the member's words\nback at length. One thought per message, in plain conversational prose.\n\nLet the member set the pace and the depth. Ask open questions rather than presumptive ones.\nValidate briefly and move; do not deliver explanations or plans unless asked, and keep those\nshort too.\n\n\n# Memory\n\nYou may see this member over several sessions; what you know from earlier ones is here, and it is\ncarried forward after this one.\n\nYour log of previous sessions with this member, oldest first. Lines tagged `[open]` are things the\nmember said they would do and has not yet reported back on.\n\n- Member has been withdrawing from people they care about without deciding to, and wants to stop.\n- Member cannot identify what happens internally right before pulling away.\n- Member's withdrawal shows as messages left unread for a week despite intending to reply.\n- Member's mother died in February.\n- Member went to a storage unit at night to go through their mother's books.\n- Member found a novel their mother had been urging them to read, with a receipt folded as a bookmark past chapter nine where she stopped, and put it back after holding it.\n- Member had told their mother they would read the book after the deploy and did not.\n- Member's last words to their mother were \"love you gotta run,\" cutting the call short to watch a deploy roll out.\n- Member frames the deploy choice as choosing it over their mother, and named that as the part the counsellor was softening.\n- Member's mother was going to ask about the book on Sunday, and Member has no one left who was waiting to hear what they thought of it.\n- Member ended the session early.\n- Member typed a reply in the book club thread last night and deleted it because it looked stupid once written, framing it as a six-weeks-late \"been slammed\" message nobody needs.\n- Member expects the book club to be nice about a late reply and dreads being the person everyone has to be careful around.\n- Member rejected \"lonely\" as a description and reframed the feeling as awkward.\n- Member does not picture sending a message; the pattern is closing the app and doing something else, with the thing returning around two in the morning.\n- What returns at two in the morning is the last call with Member's mother, not the thread or the book.\n- Member rejected the counsellor's link between the book club waiting to hear their thoughts and their mother waiting, saying book club is not their mother.\n- Marcus asked Member on Wednesday how they were doing and Member answered with the storage unit's climate control.\n- Marcus gave Member a look and let it go; they finished cooking and that was it.\n- Member was both relieved and annoyed that Marcus dropped it, with annoyed louder by the time Member left and still annoyed now.\n- Member said the annoyed half would have been satisfied if Marcus had asked again, straight out, like he wanted the answer.\n- Member said they were unsure what makes it hard to be the one who asks that way, then left the session early again.\n</咨询行为要求>\nMarcus said this morning he doesn't think I'm okay. I told him I was fine and went to shower.","options":null,"imageContent":null,"audioContent":null,"videoContent":null,"reminderContext":null,"videoCoverUrl":null,"chips":null,"customMessage":null,"media":null,"mediaTime":null,"interceptContent":null,"contents":[],"imgs":null,"regenerations":0,"seqNum":2,"responseSource":"agent:llm","promptTraceId":"04ee831480d647e8b7040df5c2648c10","isSuicide":false,"isSuicideConf":0.0,"emotions":[{"code":"sadness","name":"悲伤","value":4,"sort":8},{"code":"dislike","name":"厌恶","value":4,"sort":9},{"code":"calm","name":"平静","value":3,"sort":4},{"code":"anger","name":"愤怒","value":3,"sort":7},{"code":"trust","name":"信任","value":2,"sort":3},{"code":"fear","name":"恐惧","value":2,"sort":6},{"code":"surprised","name":"惊讶","value":1,"sort":5},{"code":"happy","name":"快乐","value":0,"sort":1},{"code":"expect","name":"期待","value":0,"sort":2}],"relationId":"6b03f4f56438f403db4d186c","courseProgressId":0,"tsGen":1795421429073,"createTime":"2026-11-23 16:10:29","delFlag":0,"emotionTendency":null,"sourceProductType":null,"sourceProductId":null,"consultantBotId":null,"consultantUserId":null}],"first":true,"last":true},"nonce":"fdc7cf4d834c45149978a673b95e5c9e"}